{#-
  DEPRECATED since 1.52, removed in 2.0. Kept only so that host templates which followed the 1.51 docs and still contain
  {% form_theme form.code '@NowoAuthKitBundle/form/mfa_otp_widget.html.twig' %} keep rendering: delete that line.
  The MFA code now renders with nowo-tech/otp-input-bundle's own widget (^1.9: a visible text input without
  JavaScript, the digit boxes once otp-input.js has bound them). The block below is inert: `nowo_auth_kit_mfa_otp` is
  no longer a block prefix of the field (MfaCodeFormType), so Symfony never picks it, and applying this theme changes
  nothing. Do not override or wrap it; with OtpInputBundle 1.9 a wrapper around `nowo_otp_input_widget` renders the
  boxes twice.
-#}
{%- block nowo_auth_kit_mfa_otp_widget -%}
    {{- form_widget(form) -}}
{%- endblock nowo_auth_kit_mfa_otp_widget -%}
